WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.663
Welcome. This is your ten-day plan for the child who reads the words, but does not take them in.

2
00:00:06.113 --> 00:00:07.247
Here is a sentence.

3
00:00:07.647 --> 00:00:09.250
A cat sat on a big box.

4
00:00:09.850 --> 00:00:13.756
A child can read every word of it right, and still not know what it said.

5
00:00:14.456 --> 00:00:17.661
The goal of this plan is a child who reads it, and sees it.

6
00:00:18.111 --> 00:00:20.262
A cat. On a box. A big box.

7
00:00:20.962 --> 00:00:26.817
On day ten, your child reads a short story never seen before, tells you what happened, and draws it.

8
00:00:27.267 --> 00:00:32.955
That is the goal. It is not a promise. Day ten is a check, and it shows you where your child is.

9
00:00:33.755 --> 00:00:38.000
This video tells you what the plan is, what to expect, and how to use it.

10
00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:44.357
This plan is for a child who can read short words and sentences, but does not take them in.

11
00:00:44.807 --> 00:00:47.851
You ask a question about the page, and there is no answer.

12
00:00:48.301 --> 00:00:51.187
You say, tell me what happened, and your child cannot.

13
00:00:51.637 --> 00:00:53.661
Or it is gone by the end of the page.

14
00:00:54.111 --> 00:01:00.517
This is common while reading is new. Working out the words takes everything, and nothing is left for the meaning.

15
00:01:00.967 --> 00:01:07.066
Many children also do not know yet that the words are meant to make a picture in the head. That can be shown.

16
00:01:07.866 --> 00:01:12.370
Here is what is inside. Ten days. One page a day, about ten minutes.

17
00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:18.877
Day one is a short check. It shows you where the meaning gets lost. Day ten shows you what changed.

18
00:01:19.327 --> 00:01:24.899
Day one also looks at something else. For some children the reading itself is still hard work.

19
00:01:25.349 --> 00:01:30.227
That is a different problem, and it needs a different plan first. Day one tells you so.

20
00:01:30.677 --> 00:01:35.934
Every day has a short video like this one, for you. It shows you what to do before you do it.

21
00:01:36.384 --> 00:01:40.858
On four days there is a sound track for your child. You press play and step away.

22
00:01:41.558 --> 00:01:46.068
The plan has one habit. Read it, see it. And seven ways to practice it.

23
00:01:46.518 --> 00:01:51.731
Your child draws it. Does what it says. Picks the picture that fits. Answers yes or no.

24
00:01:52.181 --> 00:01:58.465
Then says who, did what, and where. Finds the word that does not fit. And tells a story back, in order.

25
00:01:58.915 --> 00:02:04.045
Each of these shows you what was understood. Your child does not have to explain anything.

26
00:02:04.845 --> 00:02:10.471
Now, what to expect. The reading is easy on purpose. Short words that can be sounded out.

27
00:02:10.921 --> 00:02:14.298
It has to be easy, so that all the effort can go to the meaning.

28
00:02:14.748 --> 00:02:20.687
There is one small way each day. Some days will need a second try. That is not falling behind.

29
00:02:21.137 --> 00:02:24.165
On day ten, the check gives you one of three next steps.

30
00:02:24.965 --> 00:02:29.960
When the meaning is lost, do not explain the sentence. Say the same words, every time.

31
00:02:30.410 --> 00:02:32.901
Read it again. What do you see? Then wait.

32
00:02:33.801 --> 00:02:40.288
Here is how each day works. First, watch that day's video. Scan the code on the page with your phone.

33
00:02:40.738 --> 00:02:45.306
Then read the yellow box at the top of the page. It gives you three short steps.

34
00:02:45.756 --> 00:02:48.904
Do the first job together. That takes about two minutes.

35
00:02:49.354 --> 00:02:52.850
Then your child carries on with the page, and shows you at the end.

36
00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:56.710
You need the printed pages, a pencil, and crayons.

37
00:02:57.160 --> 00:03:02.887
And keep reading aloud to your child every day. Listening to stories grows understanding too.

38
00:03:03.337 --> 00:03:08.623
When you are ready, start with day one. It is a short check, and it takes about five minutes.
